# One Caddyfile for both the local Docker Desktop run and a real VPS later
# (docs/SAAS-ARCHITECTURE.md section 7).
#
# JOBBLAST_DOMAIN unset -> "http://localhost": plain HTTP, no automatic TLS.
# That is deliberate for lot E, which is 100% local (see deploy/saas/compose.yaml
# and docs/DOCKER.md) - it is also why SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE=0 is set in
# deploy/saas/.env.docker.example, since a Secure cookie would never be sent
# back over plain HTTP.
#
# Lot F sets JOBBLAST_DOMAIN to a real domain name (no scheme). Caddy then
# treats it as a normal auto-HTTPS site and provisions a Let's Encrypt
# certificate on first request, with no other change to this file -
# SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE also flips back to its default (unset = secure).
{$JOBBLAST_DOMAIN:http://localhost} {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy app:5000
}
